      "dcDescription": [
        "The finger ring originates from the Masai and among the Kikuyu is only worn by rich men and men who received one as a gift from a Masai warrior. The ring is forged from iron and decorated with a pattern of punched points.",
        "De vingerring is afkomstig van de Masai en wordt bij de Kikuyu alleen gedragen door rijke mannen en mannen die er één van een Masai krijger als geschenk ontvingen. De ring is uit ijzer gesmeed en versierd met een patroon van ingeslagen punten."
      ],
      "dcDescriptionLangAware": {
        "en": [
          "The finger ring originates from the Masai and among the Kikuyu is only worn by rich men and men who received one as a gift from a Masai warrior. The ring is forged from iron and decorated with a pattern of punched points."
